224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (We hardened the design with LibreLane on SkyWater SKY130, inside a 2x2 Tiny Tapeout tile. All 6,067 cells are standard cell logic, and the arithmetic is 72 percent of them. Each flip flop is attributed to the module that owns the register driving it, thus this is how the blocks were located)
/E (We hardened the design with LibreLane on SkyWater SKY130, inside a 2x2 Tiny Tapeout tile. All 6,067 cells are standard cell logic, and the arithmetic is 72 percent of them. Each flip flop is attributed to the module that owns the register driving it, thus this is how the blocks were located)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [97]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (The design closes 50 MHz with 1.955 ns of setup slack and zero violations at all nine corners, which implies 55.4 MHz at the slow corner. DRC, LVS, antenna and inferred latch counts are all zero.)
/E (The design closes 50 MHz with 1.955 ns of setup slack and zero violations at all nine corners, which implies 55.4 MHz at the slow corner. DRC, LVS, antenna and inferred latch counts are all zero.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [98]
>>
endobj
